  "body": "### Page link:\n\n\nhttps://bazel.build/external/overview\n\n### Problem description (include actual vs expected text, if applicable):\n\n\nBroken link to local_repository rule\n\n### Where do you see this issue? (include link to specific section of the page, if applicable)\n\n\nhttps://bazel.build/external/overview#repo-rule\n\nIn this section the link for 'local_repository' in the sentence is dead.\n\n> The most common repo rules by far are [http_archive](https://bazel.build/rules/lib/repo/http#http_archive), which downloads an archive from a URL and extracts it, and [local_repository](https://bazel.build/reference/be/workspace#local_repository), which symlinks a local directory that is already a Bazel repository.\n\n\n\n### Any other information you'd like to share?\n\n_No response_",
